{
  "_comment": "WIND-UP SIGN acceptance tier (docs/SPEC_phase_windup_sign.md section 8 item 1). Four config cells x TWO EXES: run once with the shipped exe (--exe gnss_processor_shipped.exe --output-root .../A_shipped) and once with the sign-corrected exe (--exe gnss_processor_windupfix.exe --output-root .../B_fixed). arm1 = A/a_wu_on_*, arm2 = A/b_wu_off_* (must be BYTE-IDENTICAL to B/b_wu_off_*, the built-in null control), arm3 = B/a_wu_on_*. Cell labels are prefixed a_/b_/c_/d_ so the harness's alphabetical A-B reference fallback (run_test_suite.py:387) lands on the shipped default. Decide with scripts/windup_ab_linearity.py, NOT with the 2 cm golden gate.",
  "date": { "year": 2024, "doy": 129 },
  "exe": "build/x64-Release/gnss_processor_shipped.exe",
  "output_root": "test_suite_results/windup/A_shipped",

  "truth": {
